data.content:
Done. Here's what the component does:

- **Generic** (`@typeparam TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Immutable input** — copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet`, never mutates the original.
- **Move Up/Down buttons** — swap items in the internal list, then invoke `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy.
- **Code-behind** — `partial class` in `SortableList.razor.cs`.

Usage matches your example (use `ItemTemplate` as the template parameter name):

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
